        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 142 adds support for the view transitions feature <code class=\"notranslate\">Document.activeViewTransition</code>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5067126381215744\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5067126381215744</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds docs for this new property.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41551",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document the Document.activeViewTransition property",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-16T16:29:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-16T08:02:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces the content on testing localizations with a link to the article created on Extension Workshop in<br>\n<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3503530355\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mozilla/extension-workshop/issues/2190\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mozilla/extension-workshop/pull/2190/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mozilla/extension-workshop/pull/2190\">mozilla/extension-workshop#2190</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41537",
            "title": "Localization testing content to Extension Workshop",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-16T17:33:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T23:45:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is a top-level page for the new authentication docs, reflecting <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1miZbXVjs070J2HH0rsDxqPnUaqNtPP51Uo8d4FU6PTk/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.kbs51irq6pyz\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1miZbXVjs070J2HH0rsDxqPnUaqNtPP51Uo8d4FU6PTk/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.kbs51irq6pyz</a>, more or less.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's basically a landing page: that is, a navigational aid for people to reach the other pages we're going to write, and to put them in context. I expect we might want to expand it as/when we decide we want to add new pages, but at the moment it just assumes 5 subpages: one for each authentication method covered+1 for session management.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Anyway, it's enough for now, to provide some structure for the pages on authentication methods, which we're planning to write next.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/martinakraus/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/martinakraus\">@martinakraus</a> , I would be happy for you to take a look at this and the other authentication PRs that will be coming, if you would like to :).</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41536",
            "title": "Authentication overview page",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-15T02:51:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T22:39:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63328381?u=94bf21f5823e17bc14d7e82e61e77b0698ad6686&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update the <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">Accept-Signature</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature-Input</code> headers to point to the RFC9421 rather than a WICG draft. Also <code class=\"notranslate\">Signed-Headers</code> seems to to not be used, so changing in favor of <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature-Input</code> which is defined. Based on <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713#issue-1142375682\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WICG/webpackage/issues/713/hovercard\">this issue</a>, the WICG http message signatures seems somewhat obsoleted?</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Points to the adopted RFC rather than draft documents</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">n/a</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1142375682\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WICG/webpackage/issues/713/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713\">WICG/webpackage#713</a>)<br>\n(<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2796270897\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37701\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37701/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37701\">#37701</a>)</p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41530",
            "title": "update signature headers to point to rfc9421",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-14T14:06:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T14:06:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "aamuley",
                "url": "https://github.com/aamuley"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chromium 141 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">precommitHandler</code> option of the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/NavigateEvent/intercept\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">NavigateEvent.intercept()</code></a> method. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134734612496384\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134734612496384</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also overhauls the <code class=\"notranslate\">intercept()</code> method page in general, adding a bunch of details in a large \"Description\" section that was missing before. I think more work needs to be done here, but it is out of the scope of this PR for me to try to fix everything. For now, I've added a bit more information about how the <code class=\"notranslate\">intercept()</code> features work so that the page is a bit more informative.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41524",
            "title": "Editorial review: Add precommitHandler() and other info to Navigation API docs",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T12:21:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T08:48:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 makes <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCEncodedAudioFrame</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">RTCEncodeVideoFrame</code> be serializeable, which essentially means adding constructors.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">getMetadata()</code> for for both interfaces with the correct properties in returned object according to tests. It also creates constructor docs. These don't duplicate the properties but link to the getMetadata doc.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510275107\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41508\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41508/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41508\">#41508</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41519",
            "title": "FF145 RTCEncodedVideoFrame/RTCEncodedAudioFrame constructors",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-21T04:19:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T06:29:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 supports Trusted Types in early beta in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1992941\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1992941</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note, experimental feature, and updates the API overview page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Its in draft while I confirm the scope with engineering.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41518",
            "title": "FF145 Relnote: Trusted Types early beta",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-14T02:12:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T02:09:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 supports returning a <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> for element style blocks rather than a <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925</a> (<code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> itself was added in FF144).<br>\nThis adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3511546094\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41514\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41514/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41514\">#41514</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41517",
            "title": "FF145 Relnote: CSSStyleProperties returned by style and getComputedStyle()",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-20T00:16:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T00:45:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232948089?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarify that browsers can use internally-available information about the devices such as user preference over ideal constraints.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">W3C specs for mediacapture indicates that ideal constraints are not guaranteed and that browsers can use internally-available information about the devices such as user preference over ideal constraints. The specs has been recently adjusted to make it more clear.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Link to specs: <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Recent adjust to specs: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3436419889\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-main/issues/1056\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/mediacapture-main/pull/1056/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-main/pull/1056\">w3c/mediacapture-main#1056</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41515",
            "title": "Clarify that browsers can use internally-available information about the devices over ideal constraints",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-14T17:41:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T00:00:58.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ahmedmoussa10",
                "url": "https://github.com/ahmedmoussa10"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In our <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FedCM_API/IDP_integration\" rel=\"nofollow\">Identity provider integration with FedCM</a> page, we mention the <code class=\"notranslate\">approved_clients</code> field of the accounts list endpoint JSON, but we don't say what it does.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR aims to add that detail.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #38259.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2867261553\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38259\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/38259/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38259\">#38259</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41496",
            "title": "Add use case details for approved_clients field",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-13T13:34:52.000Z",
